    "result": "I implemented `compare_versions` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 57 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 57. The parser validates each version with an ASCII-only regex and rejects malformed input with `ValueError`, including leading zeros in core and numeric prerelease identifiers. Precedence is handled by building a sort key per version: a release outranks any prerelease of the same core, and prerelease identifiers compare as numeric-before-non-numeric, with numeric values compared by value and other identifiers compared as ASCII strings. Build metadata is validated but excluded from the key. I chose to raise `TypeError` for non-string arguments, which the spec does not mention. I could not measure line coverage because the only permitted shell command was the test run; by reading the code, every line of `solution.py` is exercised by the tests, including the leading-zero rejection branch, so I expect the 90% gate to pass.",
